dog_walker: 1
name: Try the plugin harness
goal: Exercise project, browser and connected-vault tools in one read-only walk and review actual tool receipts.
plugins: [project, browser, obsidian]
allowed_changes: []
constraints:
- Read only. Do not edit the project, vault, desktop or plugin settings.
- Use installed tools. Do not install packages or publish anything.
- Inspect the local HTML file; this test requires no enabled web origins.
mode: auto
max_turns: 3
steps:
- id: inspect
  title: Try all three plugin categories
  prompt: >-
    Use the actual Dog Walker MCP tools, not shell substitutes.
    Call project_list and project_read to read README.md.
    Call obsidian_read on Mission-Control/AGENT_SHARED_MEMORY.md, then
    obsidian_search for "Dog Walker" in folder Mission-Control.
    Call browser_inspect with path index.html, width 390 and height 844.
    Report actual title, visible text, horizontalOverflow and page errors.
    You may call recommend_tool once to ask Laya for advice, but a recommendation
    is not required to use the granted tools. If it reports uncertainty, choose
    the tool using its description. Do not edit files. Report a blocked result
    if a required tool or connected vault is unavailable; do not invent success.
  success_criteria:
  - Actual successful project, browser and vault tool receipts exist.
  - The project is unchanged and the summary describes observed results honestly.
  checks:
  - {type: tool_called, tool: project_read, id: project-tool-used}
  - {type: tool_called, tool: obsidian_read, id: vault-tool-used}
  - {type: tool_called, tool: browser_inspect, id: browser-tool-used}
  - {type: no_changes, id: project-unchanged}
  approval: true
  max_retries: 1
  retry_prompt: Recheck the unavailable or failed tools and use the actual MCP functions. Preserve all files. If a runtime is missing, report the blocker instead of installing it.
